The ethanol directory is for a
MC simulation of liquid ethanol using the
OPLS-AA force field. The 267 solvent molecules are fully
flexible. Equilibration = 2.5M; Averaging = 2M configurations.
Time required: c.a 1 hour on a 2 GHz PC.       

Please see section 10.13 of the User's Manual concerning Z-matrices
for solvent molecules. The xSPM script is used to prepare them.

Note that the densvol script can be used to convert the computed
volumes per molecule to densities. E.g., for the dodecane simulation:

densvol -m 170.34 -v 378.5
gives the following output:
Mol. wt. (g/mol) =  170.34
Volume (ang^3)  =  378.5
=> Density (g/cm^3) =  .747334

The cmd file restcmd can be used to restart the averaging and run 4M
new configurations. This would be done if the system was not equilibrated
fully during the initial equilibration period requested in liqcmd.
The cmd file contcmd can be used to continue averaging for another 4M.

